    "body": "The supplied hardening documents referenced missing source/probe and workflow-template files, and PRES-23 omitted deletion stimuli. This completes those references while distinguishing supplied originals from new implementation evidence.\n\n- Retain four active original Markdown blobs unchanged. The active acceptance plan explicitly clarifies add/edit/delete across both Lean trees and roots; its pristine supplied original is preserved byte-for-byte under `supplied/`.\n- Add a companion source register identifying unavailable original package materials, contextual citation associations and inspectable accepted Git sources.\n- Include a reproducible standard-library probe and actual four-check result. An independent rerun also verified all 369 entries and exact 71,379-byte isolated TeX export; this does not reconstruct the author's missing source ZIP or toy experiments.\n- Add the referenced reconstructed workflow template. Its canonical 4,760 bytes and SHA-256 `70cd7e8569beb995981be210369f57c34460289e6a5890c54153683a26939093` match the independently reviewed implementation profile; original-package template recovery is not claimed.\n\nCurrent head: `6c741382c242859b5f9109d99c2758fdadc20052`. Fresh genuine synthetic CI is pending. Earlier green records apply only to their stated prior heads.\n\nAll three Codex documentation findings have concrete source fixes and independent review. #77 contains the corresponding 12-case PRES-23 regression, including research deletions that pass permanent preservation and fail the one-time maintenance scope check. The active plan still has exactly 108 requirement IDs.\n\nThis is the documentation prerequisite for #77's live base-change case CI-05. No Lean, release, dependency, application, production checker or executable workflow paths change here. Reviewer selection, settings activation, remote archival tag and external publication remain deferred by user instruction.",
